{"step_index":353,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T19:23:08Z","thinking":"The `fprintd-verify` command initiates fingerprint verification for a user. The process uses the Synaptics fingerprint reader and the `fprintd` daemon. The standard output shows device identification and a list of enrolled fingerprints. The result will indicate either a match or no-match, and return code `0` signals success.\n\n\nIf launched from the application menu (without an attached terminal), a native pop-up window can provide a brutalist biometric authentication flow, using PyQt6. This involves a background thread executing the fingerprint verification command, with visual feedback based on the result. The core application can be directly integrated with the authentication process through the main application file, or an imported authentication module.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python3 -c \"\nimport subprocess\ntry:\n    p = subprocess.Popen(['fprintd-verify', 'slone'], stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE, text=True)\n    p.terminate()\n    print('fprintd-verify callable: SUCCESS')\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print('fprintd-verify error:', e)\n\"","Cwd":"/home/slone","WaitMsBeforeAsync":2000,"toolAction":"Probando ejecución de fprintd-verify","toolSummary":"Verificar invocación de fprintd-verify desde Python"}}]}
